license: MIT

abstract: >
  A Python verification harness for the finite procedures and constructions
  presented in Paper SE-210, Operational Identity.
  The software compares an explicit quadratic oracle with an
  optimized partition-based implementation
  and exercises faithfulness, divergence witnesses,
  sibling-relative classification, regime substitution, and the
  monotonic persistence of failure under history extension.

keywords:
  - structural-explainability
  - operational-identity
  - identity-regimes
  - record-systems
  - equivalence-relations
  - partitions
  - refinement
  - verification
  - differential-testing
  - mutation-testing

